> Tags are pointers that refer to particular points in Git history.

> We can mark a particular moment in time with a tag.

> Tags are most often used to mark version releases in projects (v4.1.0)

> Think of tags as branch reference that do NOT CHANGE.

> Once a tag is created, it always refers to the same commit.

> It's just a label for a commit.


-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

> There are two type of Git Tags we can use:
  1. Lightweight
  2. Annotated tags

> Lightweight Tags are lightweight. They are just a name / label that points to a
  particular commit.

> Annotated Tags store extra meta data including the author's name, email,
  the date, and a tagging message (Like commit message)